pe=webp" alt="2024-07-10 Cal, UCLA Schedule 4 Games From 2026-29" class="w-full object-cover" style=""><!--]--></picture><div class="s-image-caption w-full sm:absolute sm:right-0 sm:bottom-0"><div class="s-image-caption__content text-default-white flex w-full flex-col justify-between gap-x-6 gap-y-2 bg-black py-2 px-4 sm:flex-row sm:bg-[rgba(0,0,0,0.70)]"><div data-test-id="s-image-caption__text" class="s-text-small !normal-case">Cal will play four nonconference games against UCLA from 2026-29.</div><!----></div></div></div><!--]--><div style="background: var(--color-theme-background-light)" class="bg-theme-background-light !mt-0 relative px-[16px] pb-[32px] print:static print:!m-0 print:bg-inherit print:!p-0 md:px-[32px] lg:-mt-[32px]"><div class="story-page__content__title-box -mx-[16px] grid grid-cols-1 gap-[16px] rounded-b-[10px] px-[16px] pt-[16px] pb-[32px] print:!m-0 print:!block print:!gap-0 print:!bg-inherit print:!p-0 md:-mx-[32px] md:p-[32px] lg:rounded-[10px]"><p aria-hidden="true" class="text-theme-safe s-text-title-large print:visible print:text-black">Cal, UCLA Schedule 4 Games From 2026-29</p><p class="text-theme-muted s-text-details">7/10/2024 10:00 AM <!--[--> | <!--]-->Football</p></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-y-[16px] print:hidden lg:gap-y-[32px]"><div class="flex w-full gap-[16px] overflow-auto"><!----><!----></div><div data-test-id="s-share__root" class="s-share s-share--horizontal w-full s-share--theme-light-theme"><div class="flex h-[38px] sm:h-[60px] w-full rounded-[10px] border"><div class="s-share-item s-share-item__text hidden w-full items-center justify-center text-center last:border-0 md:flex border-r"><span class="s-text-regular">Share:</span></div><button data-test-id="s-share__print-button" class="s-share-item s-share-item__print flex w-full items-center justify-center text-center text-[18px] last:border-0 border-r" aria-label="Share by printing"><svg data-test-id="s-icon__root" focusable="false" role="img" fill="currentColor" style="" class="s-icon s-icon-print s-icon--size-regular" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="/sidearm-icons.svg#icon-print"></use></svg></button><a data-test-id="s-share__email-link" href="#" class="s-share-item s-share-item__email flex w-full items-center justify-center text-center text-[18px] last:border-0 border-r" aria-label="Share via email"><svg data-test-id="s-icon__root" focusable="false" role="img" fill="currentColor" style="" class="s-icon s-icon-email s-icon--size-regular" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="/sidearm-icons.svg#icon-email"></use></svg></a><a data-test-id="s-share__twitter-link" href="https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?url=" target="_blank" class="s-share-item s-share-item__twitter flex w-full items-center justify-center text-center text-[18px] last:border-0 border-r" aria-label="Share via Twitter, opens in new tab"><svg data-test-id="s-icon__root" focusable="false" role="img" fill="currentColor" style="" class="s-icon s-icon-social-twitter s-icon--size-regular" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="/sidearm-icons-social.svg#icon-social-twitter"></use></svg></a><a data-test-id="s-share__instagram-link" href="https://www.instagram.com/?url=" target="_blank" class="s-share-item s-share-item__instagram flex w-full items-center justify-center text-center text-[18px] last:border-0 border-r" aria-label="Share via Instagram, opens in new tab"><svg data-test-id="s-icon__root" focusable="false" role="img" fill="currentColor" style="" class="s-icon s-icon-social-instagram s-icon--size-regular" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="/sidearm-icons-social.svg#icon-social-instagram"></use></svg></a><a data-test-id="s-share__facebook-link" href="https://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u=&amp;p[images][0]=%2Fimages%2F2024%2F7%2F10%2FUCLA-WEB-GFX__2_.png" target="_blank" class="s-share-item s-share-item__facebook flex w-full items-center justify-center text-center text-[18px] last:border-0 border-r" aria-label="Share via Facebook, opens in new tab"><svg data-test-id="s-icon__root" focusable="false" role="img" fill="currentColor" style="" class="s-icon s-icon-social-facebook s-icon--size-regular" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="/sidearm-icons-social.svg#icon-social-facebook"></use></svg></a><a data-test-id="s-share__pinterest-link" href="https://pinterest.com/pin/create/button/?url=&amp;media=%2Fimages%2F2024%2F7%2F10%2FUCLA-WEB-GFX__2_.png" target="_blank" class="s-share-item s-share-item__pinterest flex w-full items-center justify-center text-center text-[18px] last:border-0 border-r" aria-label="Share via Pinterest, opens in new tab"><svg data-test-id="s-icon__root" focusable="false" role="img" fill="currentColor" style="" class="s-icon s-icon-social-pinterest s-icon--size-regular" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="/sidearm-icons-social.svg#icon-social-pinterest"></use></svg></a><a data-test-id="s-share__linkedin-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=" target="_blank" class="s-share-item s-share-item__linkedin flex w-full items-center justify-center text-center text-[18px] last:border-0 border-r" aria-label="Share via Linked-in, opens in new tab"><svg data-test-id="s-icon__root" focusable="false" role="img" fill="currentColor" style="" class="s-icon s-icon-social-linkedin s-icon--size-regular" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="/sidearm-icons-social.svg#icon-social-linkedin"></use></svg></a></div></div><p class="story-page__content__subHeadline text-theme-safe s-text-title">Golden Bears, Bruins To Battle In Nonconference Contests For First Time</p><p class="story-page__content__byline s-text-regular text-theme-safe"> By: <span class="s-text-regular-bold">Cal Athletics</span></p><!----></div><div class="flex pt-[32px]"><!----><div id="storyContainer" tabindex="-1" class="relative w-full print:static"><!--[--><span></span><!----><div data-sidearm-html="true" data-safe-html="true" id="storyPageContentBody" tabindex="-1" class="story-page__content__body s-text-paragraph-longform text-theme-safe min-h-[200px] max-w-none prose">The California and UCLA football teams have agreed to meet in nonconference games for four consecutive seasons from 2026-29 with each team hosting a pair of the four contests. Cal will welcome UCLA to California Memorial Stadium in Berkeley on Sept. 5, 2026 and Sept. 2, 2028, while the Golden Bears will travel to the Rose Bowl in Pasadena, on Sept. 4, 2027 and Sept. 15, 2029.<br>
<br>
The nonconference contests will be the first ever between Cal and UCLA. The teams first met in 1933 and have played a total of 94 times, including at least one conference game every season for 91 consecutive campaigns from 1933-2023 while meeting twice each year from 1943-45. The Bruins lead the all-time series, 58-35-1, while Cal was a 33-7 winner in their most recent meeting in the 2023 regular-season finale for both teams at the Rose Bowl.<br>
<br>
Cal (Atlantic Coast Conference) and UCLA (Big Ten) will play football in different conferences beginning in 2024 and are not scheduled to play against each other in either 2024 or 2025.<br>
<br>
Cal has also moved a previously scheduled home game in 2026 against UNLV from Sept. 5 to later in the same season on Oct. 3, while a previously scheduled two-game series against Florida (at Florida – Sept. 19, 2026; at Cal – Sept. 4, 2027) has been canceled.<br>
<br>
<a href="https://calbears.evenue.net/events/F24ST">Full-season ticket packages for the 2024 campaign are also on sale now</a> and guarantee the same seat at the best price for all seven of Cal's home games. For more ticket information, visit <a href="https://calbears.com/sports/2022/7/11/cal-golden-bears-football-tickets.aspx">CalBears.com</a>, call 800-GO-BEARS or email <a href="mailto:goldstandard@berkeley.edu">goldstandard@berkeley.edu</a>.<br>
<br>
Fans can also learn more about philanthropically supporting the Bears by participating in the <a href="https://www.calathleticsfund.com/cal-football-caliber" target="_blank">Cal Football Championship CALiber</a> program.<br>
 
<h2><strong>California Football Future Schedules</strong></h2>
<strong>2025<br>
Date – Opponent</strong><br>
Aug. 30 – at Oregon State<br>
<strong><strong>Sept. 13 – Minnesota</strong></strong><br>
Sept. 20 – at San Diego State<br>
<strong>TBA (ACC Home Games) – Duke, North Carolina, SMU, Virginia</strong><br>
TBA (ACC Road Games) – Boston College, Louisville, Stanford, Virginia Tech<br>
 <br>
<strong>2026<br>
Date – Opponent</strong><br>
<strong>Sept. 5 – UCLA</strong><br>
